WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:14.130
Sebastián Piñera is already president, well,
actually, he’s president again, because

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.130
as you all know...

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:20.790
this political leader was President of Chile
barely 2 mandates ago... between 2010 and 2014

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:28.890
"Today is a great day for Chile."

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:34.040
Now, after achieving a strong and healthy
victory by almost 10 points in the 2017 presidential elections

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.740
Sebastián Piñera was declared president
on March 11.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:53.920
Well, dear viewers, in this video we’ll
see what kind of Chile this president is inheriting,

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:54.920
as well as

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:56.510
the great challenges that lie ahead.

00:00:56.510 --> 00:01:01.210
But first of all, let’s get to know this
character better, let's see who Sebastián

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:02.210
Piñera is.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:12.450
WHO IS SEBASTIÁN PIÑERA?

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:16.430
First of all, we need to know that Sebastián
Piñera, for many reasons, isn’t just another

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:17.430
politician.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:21.640
See, we’re talking about a man who, on the
one hand, owns one of the biggest fortunes

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:22.640
in Chile.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:28.210
A fortune that Forbes magazine estimates,
is no less than 2.7 billion dollars.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:33.790
You heard that right.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:38.620
(SUBTITLES FOR A CLIP: "I’ve always rebelled
against those who want to separate the entrepreneurial

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:39.620
spirit from the government.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:44.140
It seems absurd to me that they prefer a government
full of political

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:45.160
operators and that has no honest entrepreneurs.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:53.280
For the first to be able to run for everything,
while the

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:54.280
others can’t run at all.)

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.870
For years, Sebastián Piñera was an aggressive,
self-made businessman.

00:01:56.870 --> 00:02:02.160
But don’t be fooled by his Colgate smile...
his record shows that for a long time Piñera

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.250
knew how to play

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:08.879
to the limit and become a major investor in
various sectors, such as construction, supermarkets,

00:02:08.879 --> 00:02:09.879
airlines

00:02:09.879 --> 00:02:10.879
and TV channels.

00:02:10.879 --> 00:02:15.000
Yes, now that I think about it, it’s hard
to find a sector in which Piñera didn’t try his luck...

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.670
Even in 2006, he decided to bet on the football industry and took control of a team... but

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:22.910
not any team,

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:26.290
the most important soccer team in Chile, the Colo-Colo.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:31.450
Of course many critics accuse him of buying this team not as an investment, but as a political

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:32.450
maneuver,

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:33.450
like Silvio Berlusconi.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:42.090
But don’t think that Piñera’s exploits
were only in the business sector, not at all.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:45.890
In the political arena, the current President
of Chile also left his mark.

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.660
In 2010 he became the first

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:51.020
right-wing president to be democratically
elected since 1958.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:56.760
Piñera also became the first right-wing president since Chile underwent its democratic transition

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:57.760
after

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.850
Augusto Pinochet’s era.

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:04.090
Now, in 2018, this is happening again.

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:09.400
In other words, we could say that Sebastián
Piñera is a fortunate guy, don’t you think?

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:13.290
Well, the fact is that in his first stage,
despite having to face the consequences of

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:14.290
a terrible

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:17.790
earthquake that shook his country just 2 weeks before his investiture, his first government

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:19.790
had relatively good results.

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:24.420
"At least half of our efforts throughout the
entire administration were devoted to rebuilding

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:25.420
the country

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:30.640
and consequently, we had to sacrifice many
things we wanted to do”, Rodrigo Hinzpeter,

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:31.640
Minister of the

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:35.180
Interior and Minister of Defense in Sebastián Piñera’s first government

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:40.350
The truth is that no great revolutionary change really happened, however, in his 4 years of government,

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:45.100
the economy grew by more than 5% per year,
more than 1 million jobs were created, wages

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.130
increased and

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:47.440
poverty fell sharply.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:52.370
AUDIO: "We had a really good government, in
which every social and economic indicator

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:53.720
improved in Chile,

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:56.459
but I have more experience now, and experience
counts."

00:03:56.459 --> 00:03:57.459
Sebastián Piñera.

00:03:57.459 --> 00:04:02.010
And the truth is my friends, that in this
case, all that experience can be very, very

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:03.040
important, why?

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:10.380
Well... because today’s Chile is quite different.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:19.859
Listen up.

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:27.870
TODAY’S CHILE

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:31.570
We already told you here on VISUALPOLITIK
and of course I don’t think this will surprise

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:32.570
anyone.

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:37.360
In the last few decades, Chile has been something
like Latin America’s Cristiano Ronaldo,

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:38.360
the country

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:41.419
that grew the most, the one that had the most
success.

00:04:41.419 --> 00:04:45.819
Convincing proof of this was the evolution
of the Chilean middle class, which multiplied

00:04:45.819 --> 00:04:46.979
by almost 3

00:04:46.979 --> 00:04:49.699
times within a very short span.

00:04:49.699 --> 00:04:56.919
"The Chilean middle class grew from 23.7%
to 64.3% of the population in 25 years" Diario Exterior

00:04:57.919 --> 00:05:01.199
However, as we saw here in a previous video, in recent years, specifically during Michelle Bachelet’s

00:05:02.199 --> 00:05:03.419
last term, things changed.

00:05:03.419 --> 00:05:09.150
"Chile is a medium-sized country that hasn’t yet been able to fully develop, but its accelerated

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:12.020
modernization in recent decades has put us squarely on the frontier of modernity’s

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:13.389
challenges and the

00:05:13.389 --> 00:05:21.469
tensions that democracy and economic growth face.

00:05:21.469 --> 00:05:26.479
Just as we mentioned, in recent years economic growth has plummeted, job creation has slowed

00:05:26.479 --> 00:05:27.479
down, wages

00:05:27.479 --> 00:05:29.770
haven’t grown and foreign investment has
dropped.

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:35.199
Lately, the only thing that has grown in Chile have been the number of public employees,

00:05:35.199 --> 00:05:36.199
taxes and

00:05:36.199 --> 00:05:37.199
bureaucracy.

00:05:37.199 --> 00:05:41.699
That's right, practically every economic parameter
made a very negative change during Michelle

00:05:41.699 --> 00:05:42.699
Bachelet’s

00:05:42.699 --> 00:05:43.699
last term.

00:05:43.699 --> 00:05:44.699
Check this out:

00:05:44.699 --> 00:05:49.400
For example, there has been an average growth
of barely 1.8% per year, which implies that

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:50.400
this

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:54.249
legislation was the worst in economic growth
terms since the democratic transition.

00:05:54.249 --> 00:06:00.419
In fact, in recent years, Chile has grown
less than the world economy and considerably

00:06:00.419 --> 00:06:01.419
less than its The

00:06:01.419 --> 00:06:04.630
Pacific Alliance counterparts, Mexico, Peru
and Colombia.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.110
And that's not all.

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:11.860
The public deficit went from being a guest
to a permanent tenant, and of course that

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:13.060
has consequences.

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:20.319
Public debt, although still low, has reached
its highest level since 1993.

00:06:20.319 --> 00:06:27.069
"Having the fiscal debt double every four
years isn’t sustainable.

00:06:27.069 --> 00:06:29.270
That’s the road to the precipice"

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:31.590
Felipe Larraín, Minister of Finance.)

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:36.770
Although, by far, the worst development has
been the 4-year consecutive drop in investments.

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:39.120
And it wasn’t only the economy that went
south.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:42.569
Crime rates have increased a lot.

00:06:42.569 --> 00:06:46.189
In the Araucanía region, where there’s
a conflict with the indigenous peoples -the

00:06:46.189 --> 00:06:47.189
Mapuches, who demand

00:06:47.189 --> 00:06:51.939
more autonomy and recognition- violent acts
have exploded, growing by 150%.

00:06:51.939 --> 00:06:54.169
"What does the government want?

00:06:54.169 --> 00:07:01.940
For citizens to have to organize armed militias
to protect themselves or

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:07.779
for them to take justice into their own hands?")

00:07:07.779 --> 00:07:11.529
And even regarding health, the government's
decision to suspend the hospital concession

00:07:11.529 --> 00:07:12.529
system has meant

00:07:12.529 --> 00:07:17.159
that the government has barely been able to
invest more than half of what they’d budgeted...

00:07:17.159 --> 00:07:18.159
making

00:07:18.159 --> 00:07:20.659
waitlists and quality issues a chronic disease.

00:07:20.659 --> 00:07:26.180
And... let's not deceive ourselves, as always,
the ones most affected by all of this aren’t

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:27.180
the richest,

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:32.110
but the middle class and even more so, the
most vulnerable population, the poor.

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:36.039
In other words, it’s fair to say that Chileans
have no reason to celebrate Michelle Bachelet’s

00:07:36.039 --> 00:07:37.039
last term.

00:07:37.039 --> 00:07:41.819
Those were a very intense 4 years!

00:07:41.819 --> 00:07:46.830
Perhaps, we could see what’s happening in
Chile by taking a look at their economic freedom

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:47.830
index, whose

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:51.340
correlation with a country’s level of wealth
and prosperity is very high.

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:59.999
Well, during Michelle Bachelet’s last term,
Chile fell from the 7th position to the 20th.

00:07:59.999 --> 00:08:05.430
Anyway, this is the Chile that the new president,
Sebastián Piñera, has to face.

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:06.430
Now the question we need

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:11.530
to ask ourselves is, what should this new
government’s priorities be?

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:12.669
What can we expect?

00:08:12.669 --> 00:08:13.860
Well, let's

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:14.860
see.

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:18.479
"We need to bring the state closer to the
citizens".)

00:08:18.479 --> 00:08:22.650
"How can a government be good if it’s holding
Chile stagnant, plunged into frustration,

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:23.650
doesn’t create

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:30.710
but destroys good jobs, and doesn’t improve
wages or pensions?")

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:40.500
THE 
GREAT CHALLENGES

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:47.020
Well, it seems quite clear that in a country
that isn’t exactly cheap and in which 3

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:48.020
out of 4 workers

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:52.990
make less than USD 800 a month, the economy
has to be their number one priority.

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:56.490
If the economy isn’t doing well, social
statistics won’t do well either.

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:58.950
And this seems to be very, very clear for
the new government.

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:04.020
In fact, Sebastián Piñera, the new president,
has promised to focus his efforts on doubling

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:05.020
economic

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:09.190
growth, creating hundreds of jobs and laying
the foundations for Chile to become the first

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:10.190
developed

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:13.230
country in Latin America by 2025.

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:18.389
But, of course, you may be thinking, how can
he achieve this?

00:09:18.389 --> 00:09:23.269
"I hope he doesn’t think that a mere tax
reform will it be enough to restore Chile’s

00:09:23.269 --> 00:09:24.269
growth.

00:09:24.269 --> 00:09:25.269
He is going

00:09:25.269 --> 00:09:27.990
to need an aggressive policy to stimulate
diversification.

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:30.420
Almost half of the country's exports are still

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:32.279
copper" Ricardo Hausmann.)

00:09:32.279 --> 00:09:37.870
Well, to achieve the 2025 goal, the country
needs to deal with 3 very clear priorities:

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:44.019
Diversify their economy; improve their productivity
and adjust their public accounts... but don’t

00:09:44.019 --> 00:09:45.019
think

00:09:45.019 --> 00:09:46.320
this is an easy task.

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:50.269
To diversify the economy, to stop relying
on raw materials, especially copper, and boost

00:09:50.269 --> 00:09:51.269
their

00:09:51.269 --> 00:09:53.700
productivity, Piñera's Chile will need a
few things:

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:57.089
First, they’ll need to promote investment,
especially foreign investment.

00:09:57.089 --> 00:09:58.410
That is, attract more companies

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:02.600
and foreign capital who will bet on Chile
to produce and provide services.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:06.769
This plan could really be helped by a reversal
of Bachelet’s terrible tax reform, which

00:10:06.769 --> 00:10:07.769
not only raised

00:10:07.769 --> 00:10:12.199
taxes on companies, but also punished their
investments.

00:10:12.199 --> 00:10:13.589
Not a good idea!

00:10:13.589 --> 00:10:19.220
Decreasing the huge bureaucracy by, for example,
digitizing every process, would help a lot

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:20.220
too.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:23.850
Second... and this is a much more controversial
issue for this Latin American country... they’ll

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:24.850
need to

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:27.630
promote a program to attract foreign talent.

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:30.560
Yes, to promote immigration.

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:35.629
See, in Chile, the immigrant population has
grown a lot in recent years but it’s still

00:10:35.629 --> 00:10:36.629
very low, and

00:10:36.629 --> 00:10:38.920
hasn’t even reached 3% of the population.

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:42.140
And Chileans like to compare themselves with
Australia and New

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:46.709
Zealand, where immigrants make up to 30% of
the total population, 10 times more than Chile.

00:10:46.709 --> 00:10:48.700
Yes, my friends, you heard that right.

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:53.060
The best way to gain talent and promote different
businesses and activities is to attract people

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:54.060
with

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:57.500
different skills and abilities from all over
the world.

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:01.140
We’ll discuss this in more detail soon,
but

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:02.930
here’s a prime example:

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:07.629
In Silicon Valley, the great global innovation
center, 54% of all entrepreneurs, that is,

00:11:07.629 --> 00:11:08.670
more than half,

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:09.670
are foreigners.

00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:14.620
And no, we’re not talking about an open
door, but about setting a mechanism in motion

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:15.730
that clarifies and

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:17.339
promotes talent attraction.

00:11:17.339 --> 00:11:21.920
Because at the end of the day, if all goes
well, Chile can aspire to become the great

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:22.920
benchmark for

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:27.240
businesses in Latin America.... and that implies
attracting professionals.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:33.920
In addition, and this is an important detail,
according to all Chilean statistics, immigrants

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:34.920
have more

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:40.589
education on average, their labor participation
is much higher and they earn more money.

00:11:40.589 --> 00:11:45.029
Other policies Chile needs to enforce are
improving relations between universities and

00:11:45.029 --> 00:11:46.029
companies; fight

00:11:46.029 --> 00:11:53.050
insecurity rates; end public deficit; improve
infrastructure and increase savings.

00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:58.860
Well, if we take a look at Sebastián Piñera's
program, we’ll see that the president's

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.149
promises seem to

00:12:00.149 --> 00:12:02.910
run on this line... so, in principle, everything
a priori suggests that this political change

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:03.910
will be

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:04.910
good for Chile.

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:07.440
Of course, as we all know, only time will
tell.

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:11.639
But, just a moment, because not everything
will be so simple.

00:12:11.639 --> 00:12:16.010
See, due to an Electoral Law reform Michelle
Bachelet promoted, Piñera's coalition doesn’t

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:17.010
have a

00:12:17.010 --> 00:12:21.730
majority in Congress, so negotiating and seeking
parliamentary agreements will be a priority

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:22.730
for this new

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:23.730
government team.

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:27.639
So, my friends, that's the way things are,
but now it's your turn.

00:12:27.639 --> 00:12:30.350
What’s your opinion on Sebastián Piñera’s
new government?

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:33.440
How do you think his government will be for

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:34.440
Chile?

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:37.940
Leave your answer in the comments as well
as in the survey.

